From cc5c27dedca2f433970f9409e9819d92e4225770 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Sukrit Jaidee <45908411+SukritJaAIproject@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Wed, 23 Sep 2026 10:57:40 +0700
Subject: [PATCH 15/18] fix(desktop): review findings on the 1.3.0 branch

- worker: the ISO 15118-2 [V2G2-448] alert text also contains "no
  SessionSetupRes", so the older branch blamed the charger; it now gets
  its own neutral "communication" attribution.
- export_summary: a supplied data root that is incomplete fails with the
  missing files instead of silently falling back to the published v4
  root (which would have shipped the ISO edition with the baseline
  benchmark); the policy id is checked against the sidecar whitelist and
  its flags come from there; --train-records is explicit (prepare-desktop
  forwards IMPS_FAULT_TRAIN_RECORDS) and refused for a non-baseline policy.
- backend: the training rows are checked against the leaderboard that
  belongs to the records file (records_<tag> -> leaderboard_<tag>), which
  must exist, be split=train and carry AgenticAI.
- sidecar: an invalid detectionPolicy stops the runtime at start-up with
  the reason instead of hanging the app until the health timeout.
- job_service: --original-name=<value>, so a capture named "-x.pcap" is
  not parsed as an option.
- Stations tab / dialog: training rows get in-sample labels in the dialog,
  the note follows the split filter, and an empty search offers matches
  from the other split. Overview footnote omits the policy sentence until
  a benchmark has loaded.
- Docs: IMPS_FAULT_TRAIN_RECORDS; fail-fast policy wording.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
